'' RUN: 'with mk( n )' -- a WITH over a temporary -- destroys the temporary on every way
'' out of the body: exit sub, continue for, exit for, goto, and from inside a nested
'' WITH. It stayed on the statement's list and died only when the WITH fell out of the
'' bottom, so every early exit leaked it. Output identical to fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/with-temp-exit.bas -o tests/codegen/withtempexit.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/withtempexit.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: +1-1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: +11-11+12-12[x]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: +3-3[l]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: +4+5-5-4
